onLabel.scala","src/test/scala/example/ExecutionLabelSpec.scala"],"diff":"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..102c54e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+# ExecutionLabel example\n+\n+This isolated Scala 3.3.8 / ScalaTest 3.2.19 project illustrates four distinct\n+execution labels. `Passed(suites, tests)` carries positive suite and test counts;\n+`Failed(exitCode)` carries a nonzero exit code. `NotExecuted(reason)` says no\n+execution occurred, while `Unknown(reason)` says the result is unknown. Neither\n+of these statuses implies success or failure.\n+\n+Constructors reject nonpositive passed counts, a zero failure code, and empty,\n+whitespace-only or null reasons. Meaningful reason text is kept exactly as\n+supplied, including surrounding whitespace and line breaks.\n+\n+From this directory, run the illustrative application with:\n+\n+```sh\n+sbt 'runMain example.ExecutionLabel'\n+```\n+\n+It prints these invented examples:\n+\n+```text\n+Passed: suites=1, tests=4\n+Failed: exitCode=1\n+NotExecuted: No process was started\n+Unknown: No termination observation is available\n+```\n+\n+The application only renders caller-supplied values. It does not start, inspect\n+or verify another process. This output is an example, never evidence of an\n+actual process outcome, test run, workflow acceptance, or authority to approve\n+an action. The illustrative `Passed` counts are not actual test results.\n+\n+The executable specification checks all four renderings, invalid observations,\n+and exact preservation of meaningful reason text. To compile and run it:\n+\n+```sh\n+sbt compile 'testOnly example.ExecutionLabelSpec'\n+```\n+\n+Only retained results from an actual invocation can establish what compiled or\n+which tests ran; the commands and sample output above make no such claim.\ndiff --git a/src/main/scala/example/ExecutionLabel.scala b/src/main/scala/example/ExecutionLabel.scala\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9ea594d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/main/scala/example/ExecutionLabel.scala\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+package example\n+\n+/** An illustrative label supplied by a caller, not an observation of a process. */\n+sealed trait ExecutionLabel {\n+  final def render: String = this match {\n+    case ExecutionLabel.Passed(suites, tests) =>\n+      s\"Passed: suites=$suites, tests=$tests\"\n+    case ExecutionLabel.Failed(exitCode) => s\"Failed: exitCode=$exitCode\"\n+    case ExecutionLabel.NotExecuted(reason) => s\"NotExecuted: $reason\"\n+    case ExecutionLabel.Unknown(reason) => s\"Unknown: $reason\"\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+object ExecutionLabel {\n+  final case class Passed(suites: Int, tests: Int) extends ExecutionLabel {\n+    require(suites > 0, \"Passed requires a positive suite count\")\n+    require(tests > 0, \"Passed requires a positive test count\")\n+  }\n+\n+  final case class Failed(exitCode: Int) extends ExecutionLabel {\n+    require(exitCode != 0, \"Failed requires a nonzero exit code\")\n+  }\n+\n+  final case class NotExecuted(reason: String) extends ExecutionLabel {\n+    requireMeaningfulReason(reason)\n+  }\n+\n+  final case class Unknown(reason: String) extends ExecutionLabel {\n+    requireMeaningfulReason(reason)\n+  }\n+\n+  private def requireMeaningfulReason(reason: String): Unit =\n+    require(\n+      reason != null && reason.exists(c =>\n+        !Character.isWhitespace(c) && !Character.isSpaceChar(c)),\n+      \"A reason must contain meaningful text\"\n+    )\n+\n+  /** Prints invented examples; it neither runs nor verifies another process. */\n+  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {\n+    val examples: List[ExecutionLabel] = List(\n+      Passed(suites = 1, tests = 4),\n+      Failed(exitCode = 1),\n+      NotExecuted(\"No process was started\"),\n+      Unknown(\"No termination observation is available\")\n+    )\n+    examples.foreach(label => println(label.render))\n+  }\n+}\ndiff --git a/src/test/scala/example/ExecutionLabelSpec.scala b/src/test/sc